We go!.

49
00:02:27,220 --> 00:02:28,580
We go!

50
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:36,920
Are those giant flying fish?

51
00:02:39,060 --> 00:02:42,820
Darkness, too far away to
tell Is something wrong?

52
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:44,880
I can't see from in here

53
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:49,960
Mom, what are those weird fish?

54
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:02,000
Whoa, look at that!

55
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:03,559
That's not normal.

56
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:09,240
Ryugu Palace!

57
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:11,200
Ryugu Palace! Come in!

58
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:13,213
This is Border Control.

59
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:14,130
Come in.

60
00:03:14,213 --> 00:03:15,043
Can anyone hear me?

61
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:17,260
Hello? Hello?

62
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:19,440
I wonder what's wrong.

63
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:22,835
I'm still not getting anything at all.

64
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:24,988
You think the snail's sick?

65
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:28,537
There's no immediate call for alarm,

66
00:03:28,620 --> 00:03:32,257
but it does seem like there are a lot of
people coming in from the Fishman District.

67
00:03:32,340 --> 00:03:33,170
It worries me.

68
00:03:33,460 --> 00:03:36,377
That many wouldn't come at
one time just for shopping.

69
00:03:36,460 --> 00:03:37,777
They're dangerous people.

70
00:03:37,860 --> 00:03:39,154
Anything could happen.

71
00:03:58,520 --> 00:04:00,280
Today is the day.

72
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:02,560
History will be made.

73
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:06,360
All of Fishman Island will
be united under one flag.

74
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:10,480
Mermaids, mermen, and fishmen
must all come together.

75
00:04:10,740 --> 00:04:12,880
We must all be of the same mind.

76
00:04:13,620 --> 00:04:15,679
We've tolerated humans long enough.

77
00:04:15,840 --> 00:04:17,600
Land dwellers are inferior.

78
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:20,980
We will rule them, or they will die.

79
00:04:26,960 --> 00:04:31,940
We will erase the mistakes of the
past and forge an everlasting legacy.

80
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:36,500
Ah, ho, ho, ho.

81
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:40,980
Today is the anniversary of our
engagement, dear Shirahoshi.

82
00:04:41,140 --> 00:04:42,137
But it's no rush.

83
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:44,037
We don't have to get married today.

84
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,740
I'll wait until tomorrow.

85
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:49,668
Seems the Sun Pirates and Jinbei
have decided not to join us.

86
00:04:49,820 --> 00:04:52,291
Annoying, but it isn't exactly unexpected.

87
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:53,760
We take down Neptune.

88
00:04:54,080 --> 00:04:58,780
We take down Fukaboshi, Ryuboshi,
Momboshi, then we're done. Mu-hi!

89
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:03,160
Then his army-hi will fall,
assuming they don't surrender first.

90
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:04,440
Mu-hi-hi!

91
00:05:05,340 --> 00:05:06,960
Yeah, but that's no fun.

92
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:08,964
I want to feast on their first.

93
00:05:09,460 --> 00:05:12,520
You tell me what to cut,
and then I'll cut it.

94
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:15,920
You know the plan, right?

95
00:05:16,260 --> 00:05:19,260
We split up, conquer
one area, and move on.

96
00:05:19,620 --> 00:05:21,237
They won't know what hit them.

97
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:26,260
Before this day is done, the Ryugu
kingdom will fall, and we will reign!

98
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:43,760
If anyone can move, try to stop her.

99
00:05:53,860 --> 00:05:55,920
It seems my theory was correct.

100
00:05:56,420 --> 00:05:58,777
There's a poneglyph hidden here somewhere.

101
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:01,036
The crew can take care of themselves.

102
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:04,692
I can't miss a chance to uncover
the world's lost history.

103
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:11,077
So what if I enjoyed it?

104
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:12,677
I fought him because I had to.

105
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:13,590
I see.

106
00:06:13,673 --> 00:06:15,457
Then you are a bloodthirsty butcher.

107
00:06:15,540 --> 00:06:18,187
You'll turn your blade
on us next, won't you?

108
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:21,837
Look, these guys were after our
heads and probably yours too.

109
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:24,038
Did you expect us to serve them tea?

110
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:25,220
Good idea.

111
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:27,837
That sounds like a lovely
way to settle things.

112
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:29,737
Oh yeah, I'm sure they would go for that.

113
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:30,650
Who can say?

114
00:06:30,980 --> 00:06:32,686
Certainly not them right now,

115
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:36,517
since you knocked them out before
we could learn why they were here.

116
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:40,417
Except it doesn't matter what they wanted
because we stopped them from doing it.

117
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:41,620
Man, I hate this.

118
00:06:41,820 --> 00:06:43,761
How do we turn into the bad guys?

119
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:47,036
It's because everyone on our
crew is so irresponsible.

120
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:48,640
Or just plain violent.

121
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:52,140
Well, just look at our
captain. Good point.

122
00:06:52,660 --> 00:06:54,200
Too late for regrets now.

123
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:59,837
Speaking of Luffy, I wonder if he
came across the mermaid princess.

124
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:01,861
I'd still quite like to meet her.

125
00:07:03,300 --> 00:07:07,957
My poor little girl you things
what have you done to her?

126
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:09,617
Why stop crying?

127
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:13,157
I know we tied up your guards but we
didn't lay a finger on your daughter!

128
00:07:13,240 --> 00:07:14,077
Liar!

129
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:15,357
Straw Hat!

130
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:16,717
Luffy took her away!

131
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:18,037
My sweet princess!

132
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:19,977
I can assure you that's not the case!

133
00:07:20,060 --> 00:07:21,757
I only saw Luffy and Mr.

134
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:22,717
Shark leave the room!

135
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:26,057
Surely I would have noticed if they
had a mermaid princess with them!

136
00:07:26,140 --> 00:07:28,037
If you knew her you would understand!

137
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:30,497
She would never sneak out on her own!

138
00:07:30,580 --> 00:07:34,037
Also someone would notice if she
simply squam out of the room!

139
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:36,717
She takes after me when it comes to size!

140
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:39,280
Your daughter's as big as you!

141
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:44,110
Oh!

142
00:07:44,193 --> 00:07:45,023
Thank you!

143
00:07:45,106 --> 00:07:46,937
Why did I realize it sooner?

144
00:07:47,020 --> 00:07:48,057
Straw Hat!

145
00:07:48,140 --> 00:07:50,097
Hid ShiraHoshi inside Megalo's mouth!

146
00:07:50,180 --> 00:07:52,415
and they all left the palace together.

147
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:57,317
Come on, your highness.

148
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:59,097
You shouldn't joke at a time like this.

149
00:07:59,180 --> 00:08:00,020
That's crazy.

150
00:08:00,540 --> 00:08:02,517
I know Straw Hat has a wild reputation,

151
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:05,306
but that's pretty far
out there, even for him.

152
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:07,030
That's enough.

153
00:08:07,340 --> 00:08:10,057
Luffy may be a pirate,
but he's not a kidnapper.

154
00:08:10,140 --> 00:08:12,297
There has to be another culprit out there.

155
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:14,197
You can't talk your way out of this one.

156
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:18,257
If my little girl doesn't come back
safe, then I'm keeping your ship!

157
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:22,540
And I'll be keeping your
friends in jail. No fear!

158
00:08:22,880 --> 00:08:24,292
We're victims here, too!

159
00:08:31,320 --> 00:08:32,150
I...

160
00:08:32,233 --> 00:08:33,180
I did it!

161
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:40,960
Looks like they finished their job.

162
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:43,400
Not bad for a bunch of humans.

163
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:50,390
Whoa!

164
00:08:50,473 --> 00:08:51,900
Hey, Sonny, looking good.

165
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:56,515
Things got pretty wild back there,
but you can't keep a super ship down.

166
00:08:58,160 --> 00:09:00,757
As you can see, others weren't so lucky.

167
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:03,677
The tide brings many sunken
vessels to this spot.

168
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:07,837
It's almost like a graveyard for ships
that couldn't reach the new world.

169
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:10,740
And yet, this is a place
overflowing with life.

170
00:09:11,220 --> 00:09:13,660
Thanks to the grace of the Sun Tree Eve,

171
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:16,777
many colorful fish and
coral make their home here.

172
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:18,095
And whales, too, huh?

173
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:21,237
I don't think I've ever seen
so many in one place before.

174
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:23,837
Some of them are even
bigger than the sunny.

175
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:26,449
Even if they're tucked
away in deep waters,

176
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:29,140
whales always know where fertile seas lie.

177
00:09:31,640 --> 00:09:33,920
This place is a real wonderland.

178
00:09:36,580 --> 00:09:38,340
It's endlessly fascinating.

179
00:09:38,640 --> 00:09:42,581
No matter how much I observe,
there's always something new to find.

180
00:09:42,780 --> 00:09:44,220
So it's not just me.

181
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:48,057
Even the people who live down here
think this place is a miracle.

182
00:09:48,140 --> 00:09:49,905
All of Fishman Island, I mean.

183
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:55,817
I don't know how you got
wood from the Tree of Atom,

184
00:09:55,900 --> 00:09:59,620
but this is a fine ship, worthy
of its parts. Damn straight.

185
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:01,253
This is my masterpiece.

186
00:10:01,460 --> 00:10:04,177
Tom made a ship out of the
same stuff for Gold Roger,

187
00:10:04,260 --> 00:10:06,680
so nothing less will do for my captain.

188
00:10:08,780 --> 00:10:12,340
I'll do the ship coding for
you, and I'll do it with gusto.

189
00:10:13,780 --> 00:10:15,237
Haven't heard that one in a while.

190
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:17,120
Oh, uh, sorry.

191
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:18,817
I never caught your name.

192
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:19,780
Call me Den.

193
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:21,340
So, Den,

194
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:24,377
don't take this the wrong way,
but for being his brother,

195
00:10:24,460 --> 00:10:26,117
you sure don't look much like Tom.

196
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:28,857
I mean, you're a merman,
and he was a fish man.

197
00:10:28,940 --> 00:10:31,058
Was one of you adopted or something?

198
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:34,998
That's a human-centric way to think.

199
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:37,017
I can't hardly blame you,

200
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:40,537
since family members tend to look
so much alike on the surface.

201
00:10:40,620 --> 00:10:42,700
It works a bit differently with us.

202
00:10:43,460 --> 00:10:47,037
We carry genes from our ancestors
that can show up in different ways,

203
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:50,061
and this rule applies to
both merfolk and fishmen.

204
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:55,240
So, if an octopus mermaid gives birth
to a shark merman, that's normal.

205
00:10:55,560 --> 00:11:00,501
It just means that she, or the father, has
shark mermans somewhere in their lineage.

206
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:02,480
The bottom line is,

207
00:11:02,680 --> 00:11:06,880
nothing really surprises us, no
matter what way our children turn out.

208
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:10,237
That's why it doesn't make
much sense to us when humans

209
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:13,657
discriminate against someone just
because they look a certain way.

210
00:11:13,740 --> 00:11:17,540
See, the way you look doesn't
say a thing about who you are.

211
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:22,057
Speaking of which?

212
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:23,197
Was one of your ancestors?

213
00:11:23,280 --> 00:11:24,800
a robot, perhaps?

214
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:26,597
That's not how it works, bro.

215
00:11:26,680 --> 00:11:27,510
My mistake.

216
00:11:28,080 --> 00:11:30,980
You're human, so one of
your parents was a robot?

217
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:32,631
How does that make sense?

218
00:11:32,760 --> 00:11:33,860
You tell me.

219
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:35,866
It was a rhetorical question.

220
00:11:36,220 --> 00:11:39,237
I should have said, I got a
letter from Granny Kokoro.

221
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:44,140
So I heard all about you and iceberg
you and the old bag stay in touch.

222
00:11:44,340 --> 00:11:45,170
That's nice

223
00:11:45,700 --> 00:11:47,120
Now that is one face.

224
00:11:47,300 --> 00:11:49,540
I never thought I'd miss at any rate.

225
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:52,386
I heard the whole story
the good and the bad I

226
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:56,188
Know that my brother
died the very same way.

227
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:57,820
He lived with gusto

228
00:11:58,500 --> 00:11:59,330
Well,

229
00:11:59,413 --> 00:12:01,157
either way I do appreciate you coming here

230
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:03,711
to tell me it seems he chose his students.

231
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:04,830
Well

232
00:12:06,900 --> 00:12:08,840
Oh, you're flattering me.

233
00:12:09,780 --> 00:12:11,662
Are you sure you're not a robot?

234
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:14,777
Uh, well, it's complicated.

235
00:12:14,860 --> 00:12:16,240
Let's drop it, okay?

236
00:12:16,580 --> 00:12:18,737
By the way, I've been meaning to ask you,

237
00:12:18,820 --> 00:12:20,937
there's a dude sitting
all alone over there.

238
00:12:21,020 --> 00:12:22,314
Do you know who he is?

239
00:12:23,340 --> 00:12:24,170
Uh-huh.

240
00:12:25,060 --> 00:12:27,180
That would be the boss, Jinbei. Huh?

241
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:28,500
Boss of what?

242
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:31,061
Consider it a term of endearment.

243
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:32,860
He's waiting for someone,

244
00:12:33,060 --> 00:12:36,942
but he doesn't want to enter the
island because he's a wanted man.

245
00:12:53,140 --> 00:12:54,320
Intruder alert.

246
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:56,597
But the front gate.

247
00:12:56,680 --> 00:12:59,100
How did you scoundrels get in here?

248
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:02,417
Well, isn't this convenient.

249
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:05,397
I was ready for a fight
but everyone's tied up.

250
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:08,580
I didn't expect much from
those pirates we sent.

251
00:13:08,800 --> 00:13:11,388
Don't tell me they're
the ones who did this.

252
00:13:12,480 --> 00:13:13,760
It doesn't matter.

253
00:13:13,980 --> 00:13:17,333
If someone leaves you a present,
you don't ask questions.

254
00:13:17,620 --> 00:13:18,860
They look scared.

255
00:13:22,340 --> 00:13:23,440
I know you.

256
00:13:24,360 --> 00:13:25,595
What's he doing here?

257
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:30,929
We fought so hard to keep Vandernak in
the way, and now he wants us right in.

258
00:13:31,420 --> 00:13:33,185
And is that who I think it is?

259
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,960
Heart Jones from the Fishman District?

260
00:13:39,140 --> 00:13:40,640
What does he want?

261
00:13:40,780 --> 00:13:41,960
This can't be good.

262
00:13:42,560 --> 00:13:43,390
Heart.

263
00:13:43,473 --> 00:13:44,560
I know that man.

264
00:13:46,520 --> 00:13:48,320
He once served us.

265
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:52,100
That is, he was a decorated
soldier in the Royal Army.

266
00:13:59,060 --> 00:14:00,800
Actually, I'm set in thought.

267
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:03,277
Are you setting a trap for us?

268
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:05,780
Had an awful lot of visitors today, huh?

269
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:10,282
They're not like the last batch.

270
00:14:10,700 --> 00:14:11,680
You did this.

271
00:14:11,860 --> 00:14:13,331
You must be a cutlassist.

272
00:14:13,580 --> 00:14:14,460
Just admit it.

273
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:16,177
You let them into the palace.

274
00:14:16,260 --> 00:14:17,090
Really?

275
00:14:17,173 --> 00:14:18,003
It's our fault?

276
00:14:18,086 --> 00:14:19,857
You realize we wouldn't
even be here in the

277
00:14:19,940 --> 00:14:22,117
first place if your
king hadn't invited us.

278
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:23,612
I don't know those guys.

279
00:14:23,740 --> 00:14:25,760
I don't want to. They're scary.

280
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:28,700
Hey, you gotta give our weapons back.

281
00:14:28,940 --> 00:14:29,820
This is bad.

282
00:14:30,100 --> 00:14:31,797
We're gonna need to fight them.

283
00:14:31,880 --> 00:14:32,960
Thunder Decken.

284
00:14:33,360 --> 00:14:35,037
So you're the one behind this?

285
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:36,837
Straw Hat was innocent.

286
00:14:36,920 --> 00:14:38,917
Give me back my daughter.

287
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,697
You've made her suffer enough.

288
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:44,617
All father-in-laws say that,

289
00:14:44,700 --> 00:14:47,257
but you'll come around by the
time our honeymoon is over.

290
00:14:47,340 --> 00:14:51,037
This I suspect I'll never
be your father-in-law.

291
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:53,257
Now where did you take Shirahoshi?

292
00:14:53,340 --> 00:14:57,097
If you hung one hair on her head,
you're losing your mind, old man.

293
00:14:57,180 --> 00:15:01,017
If I already had her, why would
I bother breaking in here?

294
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:02,777
Don't play dumb with me.

295
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:04,677
You're here and my daughter is missing.

296
00:15:04,760 --> 00:15:06,177
The situation is clear.

297
00:15:06,260 --> 00:15:08,717
Someone took my Shirahoshi.

298
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:10,817
This is a tragedy.

299
00:15:10,900 --> 00:15:15,297
She's not yours and damn
right it's a tragedy.

300
00:15:15,380 --> 00:15:16,597
Calm down, your highness.

301
00:15:16,680 --> 00:15:20,240
This is going nowhere and
we need answers quickly.

302
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:26,057
Enough screaming.

303
00:15:26,140 --> 00:15:27,357
It's a bluff.

304
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:28,797
See this?

305
00:15:28,880 --> 00:15:31,897
All the pirates you threw at
her are here in the palace.

306
00:15:31,980 --> 00:15:33,897
That means she must be close.

307
00:15:33,980 --> 00:15:39,217
Even if Neptune is telling the truth and
she's gone, she couldn't have gotten far.

308
00:15:39,300 --> 00:15:41,757
Somebody help me, miss. Eyes.

309
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:44,937
One little toss and you can
track her down anywhere.

310
00:15:45,020 --> 00:15:45,857
Don't?

311
00:15:45,940 --> 00:15:50,469
Tell me love has made you so blind that
you forgot how to use your own power.

312
00:15:54,140 --> 00:15:58,460
His power? What's that?
Good idea. You know, Hardy,

313
00:15:58,760 --> 00:16:02,995
for a muscle head, you're really
pretty clever when it comes down to it.

314
00:16:03,140 --> 00:16:04,500
Well, now he's leaving?

315
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:07,360
I have a real bad feeling about this.

316
00:16:13,320 --> 00:16:14,820
All right, Mr.

317
00:16:14,980 --> 00:16:17,820
Coral Find my princess for me?

318
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:24,140
It is flying away.

319
00:16:27,740 --> 00:16:29,757
We've been in love for ten years.

320
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:32,017
Nothing can tear us apart, princess!

321
00:16:32,100 --> 00:16:34,577
Except death, that is.

322
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:38,200
And then, I had a real big fart!

323
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:44,820
That is funny, but it's
a bit inappropriate, too.

324
00:16:45,120 --> 00:16:45,960
Oh, oops!

325
00:16:49,240 --> 00:16:52,180
If I can't have you, then nobody can.

326
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:55,140
You're about to be a
big, beautiful corpse!

327
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:56,440
Sarah Hachi!

328
00:17:02,480 --> 00:17:06,320
Flander Deccan is going to
capture my precious Karoo horse.

329
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:09,000
Oh, Neptune.

330
00:17:10,840 --> 00:17:13,360
Please, I beg of you people.

331
00:17:13,580 --> 00:17:15,660
I'll give you anything you ask for.

332
00:17:16,280 --> 00:17:18,180
Just let me go after Deccan.

333
00:17:20,900 --> 00:17:23,180
You can earn my kingdom's fortune.

334
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:26,282
You can even take my
soldiers' lives if you want.

335
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:28,440
No, King! They can't!

336
00:17:29,140 --> 00:17:32,260
I can't let that beast catch Hirohoshi!

337
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:35,500
My sweetie is the not-so-little girl!

338
00:17:37,180 --> 00:17:39,660
You're quite the pathetic sight, Neptune.

339
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:41,500
But what a shock.

340
00:17:41,740 --> 00:17:44,057
I was confident that I
could take the palace.

341
00:17:44,140 --> 00:17:48,237
But I never thought the loathsome
Straw Hats would be part of the story.

342
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:49,640
He knows us?

343
00:17:59,320 --> 00:18:01,760
He's got the mark of Arlong on his arm.

344
00:18:05,660 --> 00:18:06,490
Jinbei!

345
00:18:06,573 --> 00:18:08,397
He tried to warn me
that there was something

346
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:10,397
wicked going on in the Fishman District.

347
00:18:10,480 --> 00:18:14,715
But you, how could a former soldier
of Neptune's army be the ringleader?

348
00:18:15,080 --> 00:18:17,160
Shame on you, Heart!

349
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:21,300
Shame, huh?

350
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:25,380
I'm sorry.

351
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:27,477
I can't drum up any shame.

352
00:18:27,560 --> 00:18:31,031
Maybe because I never felt
pride in the army to begin with.

353
00:18:31,780 --> 00:18:32,610
Listen,

354
00:18:32,693 --> 00:18:34,517
there's only one reason why I joined,

355
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:38,937
and that was to learn combat skills so
I could turn this world upside down.

356
00:18:39,020 --> 00:18:40,960
Simple as that. You traitor.

357
00:18:41,380 --> 00:18:43,380
You helped me set things right.

358
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:44,720
What do you mean?

359
00:18:44,980 --> 00:18:47,957
The comforts of your
royal palace have blinded

360
00:18:48,040 --> 00:18:50,628
you to what's been
happening on this island.

361
00:18:52,680 --> 00:18:56,460
Ever since I was a child, as
far back as I can remember,

362
00:18:56,700 --> 00:18:59,940
I've seen fishmen oppressed
by barbaric humans.

363
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:03,260
All right, I've heard enough of your crap.

364
00:19:07,180 --> 00:19:09,977
Pathetic creatures can't
even breathe underwater.

365
00:19:10,060 --> 00:19:13,440
And yet, no matter how many
we kill, they don't stop.

366
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:27,420
Arlong had a fierce determination to
suffocate the arrogance out of humankind.

367
00:19:27,780 --> 00:19:29,900
I deeply admired him for that.

368
00:19:32,020 --> 00:19:35,640
And now, we will restore his dream.

369
00:19:36,220 --> 00:19:39,220
The new Fishman Pirates
continue his legacy!

370
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:44,240
He was the reason I
cultivated my strength.

371
00:19:44,580 --> 00:19:47,997
I had to train until I was strong enough
to become Arlong's right-hand man.

372
00:19:48,080 --> 00:19:52,845
I dreamed of standing by his side when he
conquered the world from the East Blue.

373
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:59,060
Well, I did, until you humans came along
and crushed everything he worked for.

374
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:06,060
Oh man, I thought we
were done with Arlong.

375
00:20:06,280 --> 00:20:07,751
Can't you just let it go?

376
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:12,750
What?

377
00:20:12,833 --> 00:20:13,860
Not Arlong?

378
00:20:14,200 --> 00:20:15,277
I'm just kidding.

379
00:20:15,360 --> 00:20:18,040
In truth, I don't even know who Arlong is,

380
00:20:18,200 --> 00:20:20,317
I just didn't want to
be left out, you know?

381
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:25,620
Ow! How rude!

382
00:20:25,840 --> 00:20:28,193
I'll have you know that I bruise easily!

383
00:20:29,340 --> 00:20:33,280
Enough chit-chat, we have
business, so let's get down to it.

384
00:20:34,040 --> 00:20:34,900
Stand back!

385
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:38,730
What the...

386
00:20:38,813 --> 00:20:39,700
Shark grip.

387
00:20:48,860 --> 00:20:51,017
He's doing that with just his fingers?

388
00:20:51,100 --> 00:20:53,335
Is he trying to break the palace down?

389
00:20:56,920 --> 00:20:58,820
Okay, I am so not into this.

390
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:00,235
I'll check you later.

391
00:21:03,940 --> 00:21:06,360
Kuma, I need a favor from you.

392
00:21:12,380 --> 00:21:15,040
Is that his own strength? Yeah.

393
00:21:15,360 --> 00:21:18,831
He hasn't taken a single energy
steroid, not yet, at least.

394
00:21:21,460 --> 00:21:23,580
He just destroyed that pillar!

395
00:21:33,700 --> 00:21:35,880
Damn, the creep's flooding the joint.

396
00:21:41,020 --> 00:21:43,600
I came you for a banquet, not a drowning!

397
00:21:55,580 --> 00:21:58,240
Oh, crap, water drops! Hit the deck!

398
00:21:58,400 --> 00:21:59,560
He's gonna do it!

399
00:22:06,220 --> 00:22:07,300
Shark arrows!

400
00:22:11,680 --> 00:22:13,445
Who's it gonna hit the guards?

401
00:22:24,700 --> 00:22:26,180
You monster!

402
00:22:26,660 --> 00:22:28,340
My guards are innocent men!

403
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:30,500
How dare you shoot them down!

404
00:22:31,360 --> 00:22:32,660
Leave them be!

405
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:34,960
You deranged cretin!

406
00:22:37,080 --> 00:22:38,340
King Neptune!

407
00:22:38,780 --> 00:22:40,133
You can't do that, sir!

408
00:22:40,240 --> 00:22:43,360
Your lives are my responsibility! Ability!

409
00:22:43,640 --> 00:22:44,860
Joy to snow!

410
00:22:45,640 --> 00:22:46,680
Cinnabental fool!

411
00:22:47,040 --> 00:22:49,260
Risking his luck for lowly pawns!

412
00:22:49,400 --> 00:22:52,837
Just poor proof that you don't
have what it takes to be king!

413
00:22:52,920 --> 00:22:53,980
Kidnap tools!

414
00:22:54,420 --> 00:22:56,460
Damn you, Heart! Why?

415
00:22:56,700 --> 00:22:58,317
They're chained and unarmed!

416
00:22:58,400 --> 00:22:59,620
Damn, he's brutal!

417
00:22:59,960 --> 00:23:02,607
Also, he's way stronger
than Arlong ever was!

418
00:23:09,040 --> 00:23:11,960
One sword style bird dancing!

419
00:23:15,900 --> 00:23:17,100
Wait, boss, please!

420
00:23:17,360 --> 00:23:19,419
Can't you just move out of the way?

421
00:23:32,840 --> 00:23:33,800
That creep!

422
00:23:34,100 --> 00:23:36,276
He used his own Gourmet as a shield!

423
00:23:36,500 --> 00:23:40,180
Hey, you two, go untie
all of the soldiers. Huh?

424
00:23:41,860 --> 00:23:46,697
Our negotiation with the kingdom
it collapsed we gave them our word

425
00:23:46,780 --> 00:23:50,737
to give back all the hostages
unharmed we couldn't keep that promise

426
00:23:50,820 --> 00:23:57,517
that's so honest you're right i'm
on it My foot's in the water i can

427
00:23:57,600 --> 00:24:03,840
feel my life draining away help me
nami wait where's nami look Huh?

428
00:24:04,100 --> 00:24:04,930
She's gone?

429
00:24:05,780 --> 00:24:07,000
It's not just her.

430
00:24:07,380 --> 00:24:09,027
Hammy has gone missing, too.

431
00:24:14,040 --> 00:24:14,870
Great.

432
00:24:14,953 --> 00:24:16,577
We're losing our friends left and right.

433
00:24:16,660 --> 00:24:18,817
First priority is releasing
these guys, though.

434
00:24:18,900 --> 00:24:21,437
Just try to hang in there
and keep at it, brook.

435
00:24:21,520 --> 00:24:23,060
Always riding my bones.

436
00:24:23,300 --> 00:24:24,712
I recommend running now.

437
00:24:25,860 --> 00:24:29,240
Oh, I need you to untie
your other comrades, please.

438
00:24:29,480 --> 00:24:31,477
I'm afraid I don't have the energy for it.

439
00:24:31,560 --> 00:24:34,317
Untie the others quickly
and take up your arms.

440
00:24:34,400 --> 00:24:36,280
Don't let them do a damn thing.

441
00:24:36,760 --> 00:24:39,172
Destroy the two Tommy and the Straw Hats.

442
00:24:39,400 --> 00:24:40,560
Kill them all.

443
00:24:42,840 --> 00:24:45,620
Special attack, Green Star Rappel Sia.

444
00:24:49,520 --> 00:24:52,217
Wow, that chapter needed a giant flower.

445
00:24:52,300 --> 00:24:54,600
Such exotic flora. Breathe deep.

446
00:24:59,060 --> 00:25:00,900
Damn bunch of fools.

447
00:25:01,900 --> 00:25:05,100
I'm dying here. Come on, Zoro. Let's move.

448
00:25:08,640 --> 00:25:09,500
Listen up.

449
00:25:09,740 --> 00:25:12,622
Do me a favor and help
those two get out of here.

450
00:25:12,960 --> 00:25:14,078
And what about you?

451
00:25:14,820 --> 00:25:16,877
We're not going to make it out of here.

452
00:25:16,960 --> 00:25:18,666
Not if that guy's chasing us.

453
00:25:25,540 --> 00:25:26,980
This is a revolution.

454
00:25:27,460 --> 00:25:28,754
And you're in the way.

455
00:25:32,460 --> 00:25:33,931
Just stay with me, Hachi.

456
00:25:34,100 --> 00:25:35,335
You're gonna be okay.

457
00:25:36,380 --> 00:25:37,260
You... Ugh.

458
00:25:37,520 --> 00:25:39,402
No, you need to get out of here.

459
00:25:39,620 --> 00:25:40,857
Quit worrying about us.

460
00:25:40,940 --> 00:25:41,770
We'll be fine.

461
00:25:41,960 --> 00:25:43,700
Come on, focus on you first.

462
00:25:44,960 --> 00:25:46,657
What's up with the angry mob?

463
00:25:46,740 --> 00:25:48,280
Give us back the mermaids!

464
00:25:48,600 --> 00:25:51,365
Yeah, we're nothing but
objects to you, humans!

465
00:25:51,800 --> 00:25:52,630
Huh?

466
00:25:52,713 --> 00:25:53,817
What are you talking about?

467
00:25:53,900 --> 00:25:55,371
Don't play dumb, pirates!

468
00:25:55,660 --> 00:25:57,237
The word's gotten around town.

469
00:25:57,320 --> 00:25:58,337
We know you did it.

470
00:25:58,420 --> 00:26:01,477
We know you kidnapped all those poor
mermaids from the beach in the south.

471
00:26:01,560 --> 00:26:03,266
Where did you take them, huh?

472
00:26:03,720 --> 00:26:05,620
You've got the wrong guys here.

473
00:26:06,800 --> 00:26:09,917
Besides, what gives you the idea
that we're the ones behind this?

474
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:11,877
I mean, I will admit...

475
00:26:11,960 --> 00:26:15,431
I love mermaids so much I want
to keep them all for myself!

476
00:26:16,820 --> 00:26:19,280
Regardless, our crew didn't kidnap them.

477
00:26:19,560 --> 00:26:20,400
You hear that?

478
00:26:20,600 --> 00:26:22,697
He just admitted that he wants them!

479
00:26:22,780 --> 00:26:24,120
Will you jerk shut up?

480
00:26:24,300 --> 00:26:25,771
There's a dying man here!

481
00:26:25,980 --> 00:26:27,740
I knew pirates were guilty!

482
00:26:28,040 --> 00:26:29,158
Get off our island!

483
00:26:33,780 --> 00:26:35,857
Hey, this bottle is almost full.

484
00:26:35,940 --> 00:26:37,697
That's a waste of good booze!

485
00:26:37,780 --> 00:26:38,657
Shut up, human.

486
00:26:38,740 --> 00:26:41,640
Oh, hey, Sanji, jumper.

487
00:26:42,260 --> 00:26:45,057
Hey, Sanji, get your nose under control.

488
00:26:45,140 --> 00:26:48,200
Luffy, is that a blowfish?

489
00:26:50,720 --> 00:26:53,020
You know them, Luffy, your friends?

490
00:26:54,120 --> 00:26:56,177
Yeah, those guys are my crew members.

491
00:26:56,260 --> 00:26:58,197
Wow, interesting crew!

492
00:26:58,280 --> 00:27:01,377
Look, up there, the captain
of the Straw Hat crew?

493
00:27:01,460 --> 00:27:02,640
You're right, it is.

494
00:27:02,840 --> 00:27:06,016
You gave the order to kidnap
the mermaids, didn't you?

495
00:27:08,600 --> 00:27:11,477
We can't let all of the
people down there see me.

496
00:27:11,560 --> 00:27:13,260
Hey, shut your mouth, hurry!

497
00:27:19,080 --> 00:27:21,668
I'm gonna go check
things out on the ground!

498
00:27:26,140 --> 00:27:27,420
He jumped off!

499
00:27:28,720 --> 00:27:30,520
Hey, Hachi, what happened?

500
00:27:31,580 --> 00:27:33,080
You leave Straw Hat.

501
00:27:33,420 --> 00:27:35,240
Did some jerk do this to you?

502
00:27:35,480 --> 00:27:36,598
Tell me who it was.

503
00:27:36,780 --> 00:27:39,309
We tried, but he won't
say for some reason.

504
00:27:39,600 --> 00:27:41,424
You have to get off the island.

505
00:27:43,140 --> 00:27:45,022
That's the only thing he'll say.

506
00:27:45,980 --> 00:27:46,980
Hang on a second.

507
00:27:47,300 --> 00:27:50,317
I heard that Straw Hat had
taken over the Ryugu Palace.

508
00:27:50,400 --> 00:27:51,230
It's a ploy.

509
00:27:51,380 --> 00:27:53,457
He's out to kidnap more of us mermaids.

510
00:27:53,540 --> 00:27:57,011
He left his men at the palace
so he could go out marauding.

511
00:27:57,160 --> 00:27:58,217
I know what he wants.

512
00:27:58,300 --> 00:28:01,080
He's gonna kidnap
Princess Shirahoshi, too!

513
00:28:01,700 --> 00:28:03,112
Oh, don't be ridiculous.

514
00:28:03,500 --> 00:28:05,037
That's absurd, and you know it.

515
00:28:05,120 --> 00:28:07,237
The princess is the size of an orca.

516
00:28:07,320 --> 00:28:10,357
Plus, she's the god of the
sea's only daughter, remember?

517
00:28:10,440 --> 00:28:15,280
Some lowlife might dream of kidnapping
her, but nobody could pull it off. Huh?

518
00:28:15,760 --> 00:28:17,466
What's up with that blowfish?

519
